 "hypothesis_card": {
  "mechanism": "AWS reprices spot per instance family in multi-month waves (price-list churn is continuous: CostPulse 2024-08-02 shows 65,388 cuts vs 259,823 increases in one EC2 publication). A family whose median level rose over the trailing 90 days is in an up-wave; over the next 90-180 days its administered moves keep skewing up, so the pooled 730-day change quantiles (which average over up- and down-waves) under-cover the upper tail exactly there. Adding k*clip(famtr,0,0.4)*(h/180) to q90 only (h>=90) prices that skew; the q10 side stays byte-identical because falling families breach q10 and widening it was measured loss-negative (-0.002/-0.004).",
  "expected_observation": "Discovery pooled 0.2675 -> ~0.277 (+0.009), h90 +0.017 / h180 +0.006, q90 breach 24.6% -> ~20.6%, coverage +0.024, 12/16 origins improved; dense stride-14 backtest pooled delta ~+0.010 with ~85% of origins improved. On Holdout: pooled ~0.295-0.300 vs gate-1 threshold 0.2916, coverage ~0.78 (in band), all horizons positive.",
  "competing_explanation": "The rival explanation of the same errors: the q90 breaches are not trend-persistence but a generic under-dispersion of the 730-day pooled change quantiles at h90/h180 (any unconditional widening would fix them), and the gain is a width-for-skill trade that will not transfer. Evidence against: unconditional/symmetric widening was measured loss-negative in this lab's prior stages and the down-side (q10) widening tested here is negative (-0.002/-0.004 h90/h180) while the up-side is positive \u2014 a generic under-dispersion story would reward both sides; the gain also concentrates exactly where the trend signal is largest (rising p5 families, coverage 0.52-0.67 -> 0.57-0.69).",
  "test": "Pseudo-origin scan (12 monthly pods 2023-07..2024-06, point-in-time): up-side widening k=0.5/1.0 monotone positive (h90 0.322->0.331->0.337, h180 0.363->0.366->0.369), down-side negative; then dry run on the 16 scored Discovery origins (pooled 0.2766 vs champion 0.2675, +0.0091, h90 +0.0174, h180 +0.0059, coverage 0.664->0.688, q90 breach 24.6%->20.6%, 12/16 origins, screen PASS) and a dense stride-14 backtest over 33 origins (pooled delta +0.0101, 85% of origins improved, h90 +0.0179 / h180 +0.0075).",
  "rejection_condition": "Rejected if Discovery pooled <= 0.2675 (measured 0.2766, screen PASS) or sanity fails. The trend-widening mechanism is falsified if the holdout pooled gain over the champion (0.2886) is below +0.003 (gate 1), or if holdout coverage_80 leaves [0.74, 0.86] (gate 3) \u2014 i.e. the widening bought width without coverage. The direction claim is falsified if the h90 gain specifically fails to transfer (holdout h90 <= 0.2226, the champion's value)."
 },
